<code>assert !c.isEmpty() => \forall int i; 0<=i && i<c.size(); this.get(i).equals(c.toArray()[i]);</code>

This assert statement checks that if the collection `c` is not empty, then every element in the newly constructed `ArrayList` is equal to the corresponding element in the array obtained from `c.toArray()`. This ensures that the `ArrayList` contains the same elements as the collection `c` in the same order.
